Shared storage is available but not tested   [known, not verified]
  With it, a person's apps could run on any machine instead of all on one.
  To use it, test it, then switch home folders to it in the deployment settings.
  StorageClass longhorn (driver.longhorn.io). Test it with javo storage verify longhorn, then set storage.home.mode to shared and run javo storage migrate.
Every machine needs a file sharing client   [known]
  The shared storage works only on machines that have it, and a machine without it cannot open home folders.
  Install it on each machine, then run the storage test again.
  StorageClass longhorn needs an NFSv4 client on every node. Then run javo storage verify longhorn.
Each person's files are on one machine's disk   [auto]
  A person's apps all run on the machine that holds their files.
  To let apps run on any machine, add shared storage and switch home folders to it.
  StorageClass hcloud-volumes, one ReadWriteOnce volume per person (storage.home.mode perUser).
  Up to 16 user homes per node (CSINode allocatable count for csi.hetzner.cloud).
Groups have shared folders   [known]
  Each group has a folder its members can open from any app.
  Nothing to do.
  Folders at /shared/<group> on StorageClass longhorn.
Backups copy files one by one   [known]
  This storage cannot take instant copies, so backups of home folders are slower.
  To change this, add snapshot support to the cluster.
  No VolumeSnapshotClass was found. Install a snapshot controller and a VolumeSnapshotClass for the home StorageClass.
Home folders can grow   [known]
  A home folder can be made larger, never smaller.
  To grow them, raise the home size in the deployment settings.
  StorageClass hcloud-volumes has allowVolumeExpansion true.
